.TH BROWSER-TAB 1
.SH NAME
browser\-tab \- browser\-tab — MCP server + CLI + TUI (single bin, subcommand dispatch)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbrowser\-tab\fR [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]
.SH DESCRIPTION
browser\-tab — MCP server + CLI + TUI (single bin, subcommand dispatch)
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit machine\-readable JSON output
.TP
\fB\-q, \-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non\-error output
.TP
\fB\-v, \-\-verbose\fR
Log debug\-level info to stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable colors
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-dir\fR \fI<dir>\fR
Directory for NDJSON logs (MCP_LOG_DIR)
.TP
\fB\-\-disable\-native\fR
Force the TS path, skipping the native module (MCP_DISABLE_NATIVE)
.TP
\fB\-\-socket\-path\fR \fI<path>\fR
Daemon unix socket path (BROWSER_TAB_SOCKET_PATH)
.TP
\fB\-\-ws\-port\fR \fI<port>\fR
Extension WebSocket port on 127.0.0.1 (BROWSER_TAB_WS_PORT)
.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI<dir>\fR
Daemon state dir: token, journals (BROWSER_TAB_STATE_DIR)
.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-dir\fR \fI<dir>\fR
Snapshot/content/screenshot cache dir (BROWSER_TAB_CACHE_DIR)
.TP
\fB\-\-browsers\fR \fI<list>\fR
Comma\-separated browsers to poll (BROWSER_TAB_BROWSERS)
.TP
\fB\-\-poll\-ms\fR \fI<ms>\fR
AppleScript poll interval in ms (BROWSER_TAB_POLL_MS)
.TP
\fB\-\-fake\-adapter\fR
Use the fake adapter, no real browsers (BROWSER_TAB_FAKE_ADAPTER)
.TP
\fB\-\-dev\fR
Enable dev\-only tools such as get_logs (MCP_DEV)
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBmcp\fR
Run the MCP server (stdio)
.TP
\fBtui\fR
Launch the Ink TUI
.TP
\fBdoctor\fR
Run preflight checks (Node version, native module, config dir)
.TP
\fBrepl\fR
Interactive REPL driving the in\-process dispatcher
.RS
\fIAliases: \fRconsole
.RE
.TP
\fBhealth\fR
Print server health snapshot (calls health_check in\-process)
.TP
\fBlist\fR
List open browser windows and tabs (Chrome/Brave/Chromium/Safari)
.TP
\fBjournal\fR
Show recorded focus/navigation history
.TP
\fBhistory\fR
Query the browser's global URL history (Chrome\-family; Safari opt\-in)
.TP
\fBpage\fR
Extract a tab's content or live state (needs daemon + extension)
.TP
\fBannotate\fR
Read or write a URL\-keyed note in the daemon annotation store
.TP
\fBscreenshot\fR
Capture a tab or window as a jpeg (needs the daemon + extension for tabs)
.TP
\fBfocus\fR
Focus a tab and raise its window
.TP
\fBclose\fR
Close a tab
.TP
\fBopen\fR
Open an http(s) URL in a new tab
.TP
\fBmove\fR
Move a tab to another window (true moves need daemon + extension)
.TP
\fBact\fR
Run an action on a tab (mute|unmute|pin|unpin|discard|reload|navigate|back|forward|duplicate)
.TP
\fBgroup\fR
Manage Chrome tab groups (create|add|remove|update|move)
.TP
\fBwindow\fR
Window operations: open | set | close
.TP
\fBwindow open\fR
Open a new window with one or more URLs
.TP
\fBwindow set\fR
Move/resize/minimize/foreground a window
.TP
\fBwindow close\fR
Close an entire window and all its tabs
.TP
\fBdaemon\fR
Manage the browser\-tab daemon
.TP
\fBdaemon run\fR
Run the daemon in the foreground (launchd invokes this)
.TP
\fBdaemon install\fR
Install + start the launchd LaunchAgent
.TP
\fBdaemon uninstall\fR
Stop + remove the launchd LaunchAgent
.TP
\fBdaemon status\fR
Show launchd + live daemon status
.TP
\fBdaemon token\fR
Print the extension auth token
.TP
\fBdaemon stop\fR
Stop the daemon (launchctl bootout)
.TP
\fBdaemon restart\fR
Restart the daemon (launchctl kickstart \-k)
.TP
\fBnoop\fR
Demo: call the noop tool
.SH "BROWSER-TAB LIST"
List open browser windows and tabs (Chrome/Brave/Chromium/Safari)
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR browser\-tab list [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-browser\fR \fI<name>\fR
Restrict to one browser: chrome|chromium|brave|safari
.TP
\fB\-\-window\fR \fI<id>\fR
Restrict to one window (opaque windowId)
.TP
\fB\-\-url\fR \fI<substring>\fR
Filter tabs by URL substring
.TP
\fB\-\-fields\fR \fI<set>\fR
Field set: core (trimmed) or full
.SH "BROWSER-TAB JOURNAL"
Show recorded focus/navigation history
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR browser\-tab journal [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-view\fR \fI<view>\fR
Which journal view to show
.TP
\fB\-\-browser\fR \fI<name>\fR
Restrict to one browser
.TP
\fB\-\-window\fR \fI<id>\fR
Window handle (required for tabMru)
.TP
\fB\-\-tab\fR \fI<id>\fR
Tab handle (required for journey)
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<n>\fR
Max records
.SH "BROWSER-TAB HISTORY"
Query the browser's global URL history (Chrome\-family; Safari opt\-in)
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR browser\-tab history [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-browser\fR \fI<name>\fR
Limit to one browser (omit to merge all reachable sources)
.TP
\fB\-\-query\fR \fI<text>\fR
Case\-insensitive substring filter on URL/title
.TP
\fB\-\-start\fR \fI<ms>\fR
Only visits at/after this epoch ms
.TP
\fB\-\-end\fR \fI<ms>\fR
Only visits at/before this epoch ms
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<n>\fR
Max rows
.SH "BROWSER-TAB PAGE"
Extract a tab's content or live state (needs daemon + extension)
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR browser\-tab page [OPTIONS] <tabId>
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-mode\fR \fI<mode>\fR
text | metadata | state
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Bypass the navEpoch cache and re\-extract
.SH "BROWSER-TAB ANNOTATE"
Read or write a URL\-keyed note in the daemon annotation store
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR browser\-tab annotate [OPTIONS] <url>
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-note\fR \fI<text>\fR
Note to store (omit to read the existing note)
.SH "BROWSER-TAB SCREENSHOT"
Capture a tab or window as a jpeg (needs the daemon + extension for tabs)
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR browser\-tab screenshot [OPTIONS] <id>
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-window\fR
Treat <id> as a window handle: tier 2 screencapture (opt\-in)
.TP
\fB\-\-focus\fR
Tier 'tab': activate the tab first if it isn't active (changes user state)
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Bypass the navEpoch shot cache and recapture
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fI<file>\fR
Copy the captured jpeg to this path
.SH "BROWSER-TAB FOCUS"
Focus a tab and raise its window
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR browser\-tab focus [OPTIONS] <tabId>
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-raise\fR
Activate the tab without raising or un\-minimizing its window
.SH "BROWSER-TAB OPEN"
Open an http(s) URL in a new tab
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR browser\-tab open [OPTIONS] <url>
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-browser\fR \fI<name>\fR
chrome|chromium|brave|safari
.TP
\fB\-\-window\fR \fI<id>\fR
Open in a specific window (opaque windowId)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-activate\fR
Open in the background
.SH "BROWSER-TAB MOVE"
Move a tab to another window (true moves need daemon + extension)
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR browser\-tab move [OPTIONS] <tabId>
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-window\fR \fI<id>\fR
Destination windowId
.TP
\fB\-\-index\fR \fI<n>\fR
0\-based destination position
.TP
\fB\-\-new\-window\fR
Move into a newly created window
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-reload\fR
Safari: accept the reload\-based AppleScript move
.SH "BROWSER-TAB ACT"
Run an action on a tab (mute|unmute|pin|unpin|discard|reload|navigate|back|forward|duplicate)
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR browser\-tab act [OPTIONS] <tabId> <action>
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-url\fR \fI<url>\fR
Destination URL (required for navigate)
.SH "BROWSER-TAB GROUP"
Manage Chrome tab groups (create|add|remove|update|move)
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR browser\-tab group [OPTIONS] <action>
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-tabs\fR \fI<ids>\fR
Comma\-separated tab handles (create/add/remove)
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fI<id>\fR
Group handle (add/remove/update/move)
.TP
\fB\-\-browser\fR \fI<name>\fR
chrome|chromium|brave
.TP
\fB\-\-title\fR \fI<title>\fR
Group title (create/update)
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<color>\fR
Group color (create/update)
.TP
\fB\-\-collapsed\fR
Collapse the group (update)
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-window\fR \fI<id>\fR
Destination window (move)
.TP
\fB\-\-index\fR \fI<n>\fR
0\-based destination position (move)
.SH "BROWSER-TAB WINDOW OPEN"
Open a new window with one or more URLs
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR browser\-tab window open [OPTIONS] <url> ...
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-browser\fR \fI<name>\fR
chrome|chromium|brave|safari
.TP
\fB\-\-bounds\fR \fI<bounds>\fR
Global\-coordinate frame x,y,w,h
.TP
\fB\-\-display\fR \fI<n>\fR
0\-based display index (fills that monitor)
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fI<state>\fR
normal|minimized|maximized|fullscreen
.TP
\fB\-\-incognito\fR
Open a private/incognito window
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-focus\fR
Open in the background
.SH "BROWSER-TAB WINDOW SET"
Move/resize/minimize/foreground a window
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR browser\-tab window set [OPTIONS] <windowId>
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-bounds\fR \fI<bounds>\fR
Global\-coordinate frame x,y,w,h
.TP
\fB\-\-display\fR \fI<n>\fR
0\-based display index (fills that monitor)
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fI<state>\fR
normal|minimized|maximized|fullscreen
.TP
\fB\-\-focus\fR
Raise/foreground the window
.SH "BROWSER-TAB NOOP"
Demo: call the noop tool
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR browser\-tab noop [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-input\fR \fI<text>\fR
Input string to echo
.TP
\fB\-\-upper\fR
Return upper\-cased
